        "original_id": "d7ff1d69-6236-5f1c-9c20-1ab5996e2c4a",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- Places: Teide National Park, Garajonay National Park, Tenerife, La Gomera, La Orotava, Canary Islands, Spain\n- Landmarks: Roque Cinchado\n- Concepts: World Heritage Site\n\nFacts:\n- Teide National Park is a national park located in Tenerife in the Canary Islands of Spain.\n- Garajonay National Park is located in the center and north of La Gomera, one of the Canary Islands of Spain.\n- Roque Cinchado lies within Teide National Park, which is a World Heritage Site.\n- Roque Cinchado is in the municipality of La Orotava near the Teide volcano in the center of the island.",
